  "body": "Found in the floor review of PR #2492 (#1649, finding 3).\n\nWhat happens: the note under Flip X / Flip Y on the WCS page (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/wcs_page.rs`, `flip_row`) says \"The posted program is mirrored\" for each flip of X or Y. The post refuses some of these flips by name:\n\n- a flipped WCS that is also rotated;\n- a post script that is not verified for a mirrored program;\n- an operation of the setup that does not post in a flipped WCS (probing, turning, rotary, multi-axis, 3+2 tilted, wire or sinker EDM).\n\nPR #2492 changes the status line (`crates/ui/src/state_wcs.rs`): it names the refusal on each flip click. The page note still shows only the flag state.\n\nWhy it is not in PR #2492: `setup_wcs_flip::setup_problem` loads the post script (`Script::load`). The page draws each frame, and a per-frame script load is not permitted (#2238). The note needs a cached refusal that changes only when the document changes (`doc_version`).\n\nExpected: the note says \"mirrored\" only when the post carries the flip. Otherwise the note names the refusal, as the status line does.\n\nDone means:\n- The note reads a cached `setup_problem` / `setup_post_problems` result, refreshed on a document change, not each frame.\n- A structural test in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/wcs_flip_tests.rs` shows the refusal note for a flipped and rotated WCS and for a probe operation in a flipped setup.\n- No snapshot PNG changes.\n",
